-- title:
--   Non-∞ cusps carry unit constant terms, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L$ in $L((\mathsf{q}))$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((\mathsf{q}))$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $H$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ given as the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as its fraction field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$, and let $j \in K$, assumed non-zero, have Laurent expansion the image of the classical $q$-expansion `jq`. Then for every minimal prime $P$ of the ideal of `chartAlgInf A K j` $=$ `chartAlg A K {j⁻¹}` generated by `jInvChartInf`, i.e. by $j^{-1}$: if some element of $P$ has non-zero constant $\mathsf{q}$-expansion coefficient, then some element of $P$ has constant coefficient lying outside the image in $L$ of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the cusp-separation statement on the pole ($\infty$-) chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$: a minimal prime of $(j^{-1})$ which is not the $\mathsf{q}$-adic cusp $\infty$ (detected by containing a function with non-vanishing constant $\mathsf{q}$-expansion coefficient) contains a function whose constant coefficient is a unit, so the prime is distinct from the ideal cutting out $\infty$ modulo the uniformiser of $A$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty_xH_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty_xH_of_eq_two) in establishing regularity of the local ring at the cusp $\infty$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_mem_forall_coeff_zero_ne_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_jInvChartInf_xH_of_eq_two.lean

